  (see [PEP 465](https://www.python.org/dev/peps/pep-0465/)). In TensorFlow,
  it simply calls the `tf.matmul()` function, so the following lines are
  equivalent:

  >>> d = a @ b @ [[10], [11]]
  >>> d = tf.matmul(tf.matmul(a, b), [[10], [11]])

